From 90d58286c22db7270a769f508b3293f3be743d2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julia Klee <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:24:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] futex: futex_waitv answers a mismatch in one user access
 window

The non-blocking answer took a frame with four zeroed futex_vectors and a
timer, a copy_from_user per entry and a user access per word. One pass now
reads the array, the timeout and every word inside a single STAC/CLAC, ORs
what is odd and what differs, and returns -EWOULDBLOCK with no key, hash
or lock. The blocking half moved out of line with its frame, uninitialized.

The scan has a verdict only when every entry is plain and readable; any
odd entry or fault goes down the full path, which fixes a behaviour change
of the earlier precheck: an invalid address after a mismatch, or an
unreadable one before it, must keep its -EINVAL/-EFAULT. The precheck is
gone from futex_wait_multiple_setup() and futex_wait_setup(); FUTEX_WAIT
makes it first thing in __futex_wait(), before any frame work.

c7i.4xlarge, min of 31 batches, getuid 64 ns: N=1 118 -> 80, N=8 386 -> 89,
N=64 2222 -> 151, N=128 -> 222 ns; bad-arguments return 76 -> 63.
Off: futex.precheck=0. KUnit: wolos_futex_spin waitv_scan_*. Selftest:
futex_waitv_semantics (error order, woken index, wake/requeue/signal races).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
